  :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
  "Enlisted Admin Advisor ⊣ Enlisted Admin Governor, a REAL compiled
  `kotoba-lang/langgraph` StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern
  -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`),
  append-only audit ledger. Replaces a previously broken/fake actor:
  `build-graph` called `graph/state-graph-builder`, a function that
  never existed in `kotoba-lang/langgraph`; `run-request!` was a
  literal stub returning `{:stub true ...}` and never touched a
  compiled graph; `store/add-record!` existed but was dead code, only
  ever called from tests. Now: a genuine `interrupt-before
  #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer pauses escalated
  requests for real human sign-off (`approve!` resumes the SAME
  compiled graph via the graph's own `:request-approval -> :commit`
  edge, not a hand-rolled parallel commit path), and BOTH `:commit`
  and `:hold` durably append to the real audit ledger (`store/add-
  record!`) — a held HARD-violation proposal is now also queryable
  audit history, not silently discarded. Store gained a `DatomicStore`
  (via `kotoba-lang/langchain-store`, no hand-rolled EDN-blob codec)
  alongside `MemStore`, proven ≡ by a new store-contract test. Four
  ops (`:schedule-training` / `:log-readiness-report` /
  `:draft-correspondence` / `:process-leave-request`), all `:effect
  :propose` only. HARD invariants (unregistered enlisted member,
  non-`:propose` effect, closed scope-boundary allowlist covering
  personnel deployment/command authority/weapons/targeting/classified
  operations/lethal decisions) always `:hold`; escalation invariants
  (below-threshold readiness, active-status leave, low confidence,
  training/correspondence ops) always require human sign-off. 18
  tests / 69 assertions green, clj-kondo 0 errors."
  :itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isco-0310"
